  "notes": "Modified cash basis (recorded as cash). Governmental funds General, Street, CRA; business-type Water, Sewer. The FY2023 governmental funds statement carries capital assets and depreciation, so the governmental roll-forward is on fund balance (p5): 2,394,308 + 677,958 - 346,110 + 75,000 - 75,000 = 2,726,156. Cash recorded separately where printed (p3: cash + county treasurer; CDs as investments; beginning from the 2022 Total column); cash does not roll with the statement because of capital assets/depreciation. Business-type: net position (Statement of Activities p2 and proprietary statement p7, same modified cash figures) 1,121,890 + 305,418 - 242,717 = 1,184,591; receipts total computed (operating revenues + interest income). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3; totals equal the government-wide governmental column), business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary-basis budget-and-actual schedule (pp8-9), so detail is per-fund lines from the fund statements (p4, p7); budget schedule not recorded. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
